    ],
    "lyrics": {
      "text": "Tru-ly, all___ things are van-i-ty, and life__ is a shad-ow and a dream. For in vain__ doth eve-ry earth-born man dis-qui-et him-self, as the Scrip-ture saith. When___ we have gained the world, then shall we take up our a-bode in the grave, where there are kings and beg-gars a-like. Where-fore, O Christ God, grant rest un-to them that have been__ trans-lat-ed, since Thou__ art the Friend of__ man.__\n\nO_ all-ho-ly The--o-to-kos, do thou not a-ban-don me for as long as I live; do thou not en-trust me to an-y hu-man__ pro-tec-tion, but do thou thy-self de-fend and have mer--cy on me.__"
    }
  }
}